# Managed by ansible (tomblancdev.wolf).
#
# The seat engine's virtual controllers report the vendor and product ids of
# the real hardware they imitate — its Xbox pad is byte-identical to a real
# Microsoft one (045E:02EA), its DualSense to a real Sony one (054C:0CE6) — so
# filtering on ids would blind this host to genuine controllers as well. Only
# the NAME tells them apart, and every device the engine makes is named for
# it.
#
# What this is for: a host where something ELSE enumerates input devices and
# would grab a seat's pad — a desktop session, a game launcher sitting beside
# the engine. One person's controller driving another person's game is what
# this prevents. On a host that runs nothing but the engine there is nothing
# to leak into, and this file is not installed.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="Wolf *", ENV{ID_INPUT}="", ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}="", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}="", ENV{ID_INPUT_MOUSE}="", TAG-="uaccess"
